  <revision rev="6" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>c3850eadae234812db3c5259d269665b</srcmd5>
    <version>3.4.5</version>
    <time>1785944951</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Build the whole fastmcp monorepo from one source package.

python-fastmcp now produces python3NN-fastmcp, python3NN-fastmcp-slim and the
newly packaged python3NN-fastmcp-remote from the single upstream fastmcp sdist,
which already contains all three distributions.

MUST BE ACCEPTED TOGETHER WITH the delete request for python-fastmcp-slim: that
source package built python3NN-fastmcp-slim until now, and accepting this
request alone would leave Factory with two sources producing the same binary.

The slim binary package is unchanged. Diffed against the currently published
python313-fastmcp-slim: 891 site-packages files identical, 39 requires
identical - so nothing consuming it breaks. Binary names are unchanged too;
python3NN-fastmcp-remote is the only addition.

This retires the release lockstep between the two source packages, which had to
be bumped and staged together for every upstream release. It also lets the slim
subpackage ship a license file, which the standalone fastmcp_slim sdist does not
contain at all.</comment>
    <requestid>1369572</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>251026a5f8cacf5c21e23febf39129ce</srcmd5>
    <version>3.4.6</version>
    <time>1786304478</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 3.4.6

Backports trusted-proxy support for the SSRF-protected OAuth metadata and
JWKS fetches: deployments can route these through a mandated corporate proxy
while preserving custom CA certificates, and FastMCP now refuses the fetch
when no proxy is configured rather than performing an unprotected direct
request.

Built and verified on aarch64: 7 subpackages, rpmlint 2 errors / 46 warnings /
2 badness -- identical to the current baseline (the two errors are the known
no-dependency-on python-base false positives). source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370144</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
